"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":2689,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":333,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["autopep8","code","codeformatter","formatter","gofmt","hacktoberfest","pre-commit-hook","python","yapf"],"visibility":"public","forks":2689,"open_issues":333,"watchers":41219,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/pulls/4872","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/black/pull/4872","diff_url":"https://github.com/psf/black/pull/4872.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/psf/black/pull/4872.patch","merged_at":"2025-12-02T15:30:56Z"},"body":"<!-- Hello! Thanks for submitting a PR. To help make things go a bit smoother\r\n     we would appreciate that you go through this template. -->\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nCloses #4731\r\nCloses #3608\r\nCloses #4873 \r\n\r\nBlack was crashing with a parsing error when multiple `# fmt: skip` comments appeared in multi-part if-clauses. The crash occurred because when the second `# fmt: skip` was processed, its `prev_sibling` could include a `STANDALONE_COMMENT` node created by the first `# fmt: skip`. Since these synthetic nodes don't include trailing newlines (those are added later in the formatting pipeline), when the nodes were joined together via `str()`, they'd concatenate on the same line, producing invalid Python syntax that couldn't be parsed.\r\n\r\nThe fix ensures that any `STANDALONE_COMMENT` nodes in `ignored_nodes` have trailing newlines before being stringified. This is done right before the join operation in `_handle_regular_fmt_block()`. The approach is similar to what was suggested in the issue, but processes all nodes in `ignored_nodes` (not just the first) and includes a check to avoid adding duplicate newlines.\r\n\r\nThe existing cleanup logic that strips trailing newlines from `hidden_value` if it ends with a NEWLINE leaf continues to work as expected.\r\n\r\n### Checklist - did you ...\r\n\r\n<!-- If any of the following items aren't relevant for your contribution,\r\n     please still tick them so we know you've gone through the checklist.\r\n\r\n     - Please familiarize yourself with Black's stability policy, linked\r\n       below. Code style changes are only allowed under the `--preview` flag\r\n       until maintainers move them to stable in the next calendar year.\r\n     - All user-facing changes should get a changelog entry. If this isn't\r\n       user-facing, signal to us that this should get the magical label to\r\n       silence the check.\r\n     - Tests are required for all bugfixes and new features.\r\n     - Documentation changes are necessary for most formatting changes and\r\n       other enhancements. -->\r\n\r\n- [x] Implement any code style changes under the `--preview` style, following the\r\n      stability policy?\r\n- [x] Add an entry in `CHANGES.md` if necessary?\r\n- [x] Add / update tests if necessary?\r\n- [x] Add new / update outdated documentation?\r\n\r\n<!-- Just as a reminder, everyone in all psf/black spaces, including PRs, must\r\n     follow the PSF Code of Conduct (link below).\r\n\r\n     Finally, thanks once again for your time and effort. If you have any\r\n     feedback regarding your experience contributing here, please let us know!\r\n\r\n     Helpful links:\r\n\r\n     - PSF COC: https://www.python.org/psf/conduct/\r\n     - Contributing docs: https://black.readthedocs.io/en/latest/contributing/index.html\r\n     - Chat on Python Discord: https://discord.gg/RtVdv86PrH\r\n     - Stability policy: https://black.readthedocs.io/en/latest/the_black_code_style/index.html -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/issues/4872/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/issues/4872/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":21309291442,"node_id":"REFE_lADOB3dpmM7FYI5WzwAAAAT2Ifuy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/issues/events/21309291442","actor":{"login":"cobaltt7","id":61329810,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzI5ODEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61329810?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7","html_url":"https://github.com/cobaltt7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenced","commit_id":"1b342ef5b0433fc1ed61a7e05a65744bef706fc9","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/commits/1b342ef5b0433fc1ed61a7e05a65744bef706fc9","created_at":"2025-12-02T15:30:57Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":21309291547,"node_id":"CE_lADOB3dpmM7FYI5WzwAAAAT2Ifwb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/black/issues/events/21309291547","actor":{"login":"cobaltt7","id":61329810,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzI5ODEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61329810?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cobaltt7","html_url":"https://github.com/cob